WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- Let's finish things up
(audience clapping)

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.730
with a story of hope on this Friday.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.966
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:07.020
- Yeah!
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.160
Jilted brides.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.260
It is a stuff of many rom-coms

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.360
and I want you to see
how one British woman

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.190
made the most of her wedding day,

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.259
just hours after learning the groom

00:00:16.259 --> 00:00:18.993
would not be making an appearance.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.703
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:35.880
(audience cheering)

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.200
I mean, that is literally,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.600
we are watching lemons
being turned into lemonade

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.360
with tequila.
(audience laughs)

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.410
We have her on the line now.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.310
I cannot wait to talk to her.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.870
Dialed in from Wales.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.312
What's up Kayley?

00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:49.011
(audience cheering)

00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:51.450
- Hi! Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.740
- No, absolutely!

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.230
Oh my gosh, you are a
half glass full girl.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.240
So I think most brides
would be devastated.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.653
How did you bounce back?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.010
- To be fair, it was just more
about what the day become.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.740
It was learning what true kind of self is

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.690
and that's what true love is

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.490
and kind of like, and self-love.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.840
That's what I learned from that day,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.900
and kind of, so...

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.733
What happened?

00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:18.660
So me and my groom, my ex,

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.320
basically planned this
wedding day for two years,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.690
and me and my girlfriends

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.550
were in an Airbnb the night before,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.710
and we woke up with so much girl energy,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.750
and we were getting ready, and kind of,

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.780
I put my like Charlotte
Tilbury foundation on

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.920
and any girl knows that it's
expensive and it's beautiful.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.650
So I was kind of ready to get that on,

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:45.000
and I spoke to his dad,
who informed me that,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.270
unfortunately, my ex wouldn't be able,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.300
basically wouldn't come
and didn't wanna come.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.900
And I was about to get
married in an hour and a half.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.010
And
- My gosh!

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.050
I spoke with my sister,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.270
I know! I spoke with my sister

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:05.250
and she kind of dusted me
off and we decided that,

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.290
I decided I still wanted to enjoy the day

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.780
because I worked my
socks off for this day,

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.632
and I was excited to
spend time with my friends

00:02:10.632 --> 00:02:15.632
and my family and I was looking
forward to the nacho bar

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.140
and the food and the
cheese and the jalapenos.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.700
And it just turned
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.203
into this incredible day.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.780
- We can totally be friends
(Kayley laughing)

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.000
just from you having a nacho bar.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.400
So tell us about your
re-imagined wedding though.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.233
Like how did it go?

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:31.500
Because I can imagine like,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.960
everyone there probably
took their cue from you

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.390
like emotionally where you
were, like what was going on,

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.550
but also that's, it's an intense moment.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.410
So how did it all play out?

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.200
- Yeah, it was hard
like for anybody there,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.810
so like guests, myself, my friends,

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.910
my family, it was hard overall.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:52.500
But once I got down there
after getting kind of redone,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.260
I had my sister and my best friend

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.600
go into the room to tell the guests.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.460
They came out into the kind of courtyard

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.140
and I walked around the bush.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.360
We gave a kind of a massive
hug, massive cuddle.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.465
Everyone had a bit of a cry.

00:03:04.465 --> 00:03:06.330
And then I said, "Let's do this."

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.500
And we walked into the marquee.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.080
I walked in with my
bride and the groomsmen

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.390
and we walked into Lizzo's "Good as Hell,"

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.100
which was just amazing.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.585
I think that set the tone

00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:17.010
- Yeah.
for the day.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.460
And I just made sure that the
playlist was turned around.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.880
So we had like independent
divas, like really iconic songs,

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.620
like you, for example, like your song,

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.600
like, "What Doesn't Kill
You Makes You Stronger,"

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.730
was just the epitome of the day,

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.741
- Awww!
if that makes any sense.

00:03:31.741 --> 00:03:32.574
(audience cheering)

00:03:32.574 --> 00:03:35.700
And it was just, like, incredible.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.510
I got a dance with my dad,
my brothers and my mum,

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:43.806
and I even punched the top
of my wedding cake off.

00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:46.110
(Kelly and audience laughing)
And it was just

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.850
a day that I will always remember

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.780
with like, pure happiness
in a strange way.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.920
- I know, but way to-

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.050
I mean, it just says
a lot about your heart

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.910
and your character and your mindset.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.770
Like, way to turn that around and go-

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.410
'Cause honestly, like you
don't want that dude to show up

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.243
if he didn't wanna be there.

00:04:02.243 --> 00:04:03.076
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:03.909
You don't want to be,

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:04.920
- No.
and he don't deserve you.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.010
The fact that you could
have spent a lifetime

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.620
with someone who could
take something devastating

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.240
and turn that around.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.610
Like, that's incredibly
hard to do in a relationship

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.620
when times are hard,
and when times are hard,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.810
you seem like a person
that is so resilient.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.370
Thank you so much, Kayley.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.652
I love you and I'm liking
your post right now.

00:04:22.652 --> 00:04:24.172
- Thank you.
(bell dings)

00:04:24.172 --> 00:04:25.773
Thank you so much.
(audience cheering)

00:04:25.773 --> 00:04:26.623
(Kayley laughing)

00:04:26.623 --> 00:04:28.590
- And that's not all, Kayley.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.960
Our season-long partner
Pilot, pen makers of FriXion,

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.850
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.670
want to celebrate your
positive approach and spirit.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.885
So they're giving you a thousand
dollars just for being you.

00:04:37.885 --> 00:04:40.640
(audience cheering)

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.930
- Thank you so much! What?

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.180
Absolutely! Thank you, Kayley!
- Thank you!

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.250
Have a wonderful 2023
(audience cheering)

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.750
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.753
Marcia Gay Harden, Storm Reid,
Holly Laessig, Jess Wolf,

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:53.749
Sophie and Ryan.
(audience cheering)

00:04:53.749 --> 00:04:54.582
Y'all have a great day.
(audience cheering)

00:04:54.582 --> 00:04:56.131
If it's not, be like Kayley.
(audience cheering)

00:04:56.131 --> 00:04:56.964
Just change it!

